["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/eli", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[European Legislation Identifier (ELI)](https://eur-lex.europa.eu/content/help/eurlex-content/eli.html) is a Uniform Resource Identifier (URI) that uniquely identifies a legal resource, typically consisting of a document type, adoption year, and document number (e.g., `http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Dataset/DatasetType/other", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "Data is of a type not included in this list.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/iscc", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/FunctionalSafety/EvaluationResultType/inconclusive", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "Inconclusive refers to a result or outcome from a verification, test, or analysis that cannot be clearly classified as either positive (successful, pass) or negative (failed, reject). An inconclusive result means there was not enough clear evidence, data, or signal to make a definitive determination, and further investigation or additional testing is necessary. An inconclusive result always shall need a comment on it.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/SupplyChain/AssemblyAction", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#nodeKind", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#IRI", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/Bundle", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#property", "_:Ne806a77768164ee1aed07ba292305fac", "localId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/iscc", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[International Standard Content Code (ISCC)](https://iscc.io/) is a content-derived identifier standardized by [ISO 24138](https://www.iso.org/standard/77899.html) for identifying digital assets. ISCC can be used in conjunction with other schemes, such as DOI, ISAN, ISBN, ISRC, ISSN and ISWC. A standard ISCC-CODE is build from multiple ISCC-UNITs. Each unit serve a different purpose. An ISCC-CODE typically look like `ISCC:KACT4EBWK27737D2AYCJRAL5Z36G76RFRMO4554RU26HZ4ORJGIVHDI`.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/SupplyChain/ResponsibilityType/custody", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "Custody refers to the responsibility, control, and safekeeping of an asset, person, or legal entity. It involves both physical possession and legal authority over something or someone.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/AI/modelExplainability", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty", "globalId", "", ""]
